namespace trion:
    use formal
    use software

    section "A proof is about contracts":
        The mapping of a statement means the contract that the language rules give to the statement.
        No proof obligation states the mapping of a statement.
        A person reads a statement as English.

        [LIMIT-SELF-HOSTING]
        The trioc command shall not report a result about the specification of trion as a proof of the language rules.

    section "Correctness reaches the references and no further":
        A real need means a need that a person has outside each specification.

        [LIMIT-NO-VALIDITY]
        The trioc command shall not report a result as a proof of the validity of a specification.

        A vacuous trigger means a trigger that the system controls and that no statement requires.
        Each response that avoids a vacuous trigger satisfies each contract of the vacuous trigger.

    section "A contract judges one behavior at a time":
        A hyperproperty means a property that compares behaviors.
        A possibility means a property that requires an ability of a system.
        No contract states a hyperproperty.
        No contract states a possibility.
        No statement adds a behavior to the behaviors that a specification allows.

    section "One contract for each sentence":
        A context-dependent expression means an expression whose meaning depends on the surrounding sentences.
        No statement holds a context-dependent expression.

    section "A term has only the relations that a specification states":
        No term has a relation that no statement of the specification states.

    section "Some proof obligations stay open":
        An open proof obligation means a proof obligation that the trioc command fails to decide.
        Some specifications have an open proof obligation.

    section "The system is declared":
        No proof obligation checks a system declaration.
        Each contract frames exactly one system.
